#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:87
msgid "Scoped performance examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:89
msgid ""
"The source release material reports the following examples. They should "
"be reproduced with the same model, backend, software versions, and "
"benchmark configuration before being used for capacity planning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:91
msgid ""
"**TopK on NVIDIA A100:** For an input shape of `[64, 129280]` and "
"`k=1024`, the reported runtime decreased from `0.353280 ms` for the non-"
"TLE FlagGems implementation to `0.130048 ms`, or approximately `2.717x` "
"faster in that test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:92
msgid ""
"**KDA on NVIDIA H800:** For BF16 with `K=V=128`, `BT=16`, and the stated "
"two-stage configuration, the reported geometric-mean result was "
"approximately `1.380x` relative to the FlashKDA comparison."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:93
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Hy3 on NVIDIA H20:** With eight NVIDIA H20 141 GB GPUs and concurrency "
"64, selected FlagGems operators produced reported throughput improvements"
" of 7.2%, 4.6%, and 3.2% for 4K/1K, 16K/1K, and 32K/1K input/output "
"lengths, respectively. The test retained four selected operators and used"
" native vLLM implementations for the remaining operators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:95
msgid "Arm CPU inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:97
msgid "FlagTree-CPU v0.1.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:99
msgid ""
"FlagTree-CPU is introduced as an independent compilation component for "
"CPU targets. The release is based on `triton-cpu 3.7.2` and adds Arm64 "
"compilation paths for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:101
msgid "SME2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:102
msgid "SVE2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:103
msgid "NEON I8MM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:105
msgid ""
"The component can generate low-bit operator instructions for W4A8 and "
"W8A8 workloads. In the FlagOS deployment path, FlagTree-CPU is used with "
"FlagGems ARM operators and vLLM-Plugin-FL. The supported instruction path"
" depends on the target processor and the compiled operator set; the "
"release does not imply support for every Arm CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:107
msgid ""
"The inference work described for this release includes weight pre-"
"packing, operator fusion, reuse of compiled kernels, prefill matrix "
"multiplication, decode-time weight access, and single-stream scheduling. "
"These optimizations are workload-specific."
msgstr ""

