#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:167
msgid ""
"The source release material lists a unified test set of 121 Triton "
"operators and identifies NVIDIA, Ascend, Iluvatar CoreX, Moore Threads, "
"and Enflame backends as current targets. Debugger and profiler "
"capabilities may differ between backends because collection is "
"implemented by backend-specific adapters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:169
msgid "Kernel generation and evaluation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:171
msgid ""
"FlagOS 2.2 continues the KernelGen workflow for generating and validating"
" operator implementations. The release material reports 1,509 generated "
"operators and 1,231 operators that passed accuracy validation for the "
"stated quarterly period. It separately reports 436 KernelGen-tagged pull "
"requests in a FlagGems release comparison; these are different measures "
"and should not be added together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:173
msgid ""
"KernelGenBench v0.2.0 adds multi-chip baselines, chip identification, "
"token-usage analysis, and anti-cheating checks. It also adds 50 matrix-"
"multiplication shapes in two precisions, for 100 benchmark cases in that "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:175
msgid "Day 0 models and deployment resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:177
msgid ""
"FlagOS 2.2 reports seven Day 0 model adaptation examples, with a single "
"model covering up to 12 platforms or devices in the stated release "
"inventory. Examples include Hy3, Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, "
"GLM-5.3-Flash, MiniCPM5-2B, Xing4.0-29B-A4B, and Qwen-Image-2.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/whats_new.md:179
msgid ""
"FlagRelease provides more than 300 model images through the release "
"channels described in the source material. The available image, model-"
"card, and deployment configuration should be checked in the relevant "
"channel before use because platform coverage varies by model."
msgstr ""

